# node_modules is intentionally NOT ignored — committed on purpose so the
# Windows install works with zero internet access at setup time (git clone
# is the only network dependency). Every dependency used to be pure JS, no
# native/compiled binaries — that's no longer quite true: `koffi` (added for
# the optional DS-K2802 card-reader integration, src/cardSdk.js) is a real
# native FFI addon, obtained normally through npm like every other
# dependency here (not a special case). Its Linux binary (this dev box's
# platform) commits fine as part of node_modules like anything else; the
# Windows binary needs its own npm install pass on that platform (see
# README) since a single `npm install` only ever fetches the binary for the
# machine it runs on, not every platform at once.

.env
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
data/snapshots/
data/backups/
data/app.log*
.gitnexus

# Hikvision's own proprietary Device Network SDK, needed for the optional
# DS-K2802 card-reader integration (src/cardSdk.js) to run on Windows.
# Sourced from an unofficial third-party GitHub mirror during development
# (Hikvision's own download portal needs an interactive account signup) --
# deliberately NOT committed pending a decision on redistributing Hikvision's
# compiled binaries from this PUBLIC repo. See README's card-reader section.
vendor/
